diff --git a/doc/_docstrings/objects.Perc.rst b/doc/_docstrings/objects.Perc.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..485137f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/_docstrings/objects.Perc.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+The default transform computes quartiles and endpoints for each group:
+
+.. plot::
+
+    penguins = load_dataset("penguins")
+    so.Plot(penguins, x="species", y="body_mass_g").add(so.Range(), so.Perc())
+
+Use an integer to request a different number of evenly spaced levels, or pass
+the levels explicitly:
+
+.. plot::
+
+    penguins = load_dataset("penguins")
+    p = so.Plot(penguins, x="species", y="body_mass_g")
+    p.add(so.Dots(), so.Perc(3))
+    p.add(so.Dots(), so.Perc([10, 50, 90]))
+
+Combine :class:`Range` with `Perc` to show an interval between percentile levels:
+
+.. plot::
+
+    penguins = load_dataset("penguins")
+    so.Plot(penguins, x="species", y="body_mass_g").add(
+        so.Range(), so.Perc([10, 90])
+    )
